# **Personal Finance Management System Development**

You will develop a Python application for a Personal Finance Management System that will enable people to keep track of their expenses and budgeting and predict their future savings.


## **Context and Role**

 As a Python developer working on an AI-powered financial management application, my responsibility would be to design and develop a smart, scalable, and user-friendly system that helps users manage their finances effectively through intelligent expense tracking, budget management, and predictive analytics.


## **Objective**

You will develop a Python application for a Personal Finance Management System that will enable people to keep track of their expenses and budgeting and predict their future savings.

## **Input Data**
 1. User Expense Records containing the following fields:
 • user id
 • date of expense
 • amount
 • category
 • description
 • method of payment
 • currency

 2. Budget Configuration Data containing: 
   • user_id
   • month
 • category
 • budget limit
 • current spending

## **Data Processing Requirements**
• Clean and standardize all financial datasets provided by users
• Consolidate expenditure and budget information using common identifiers like user_id and matching dates.
• Address any missing or incomplete entries in the financial dataset appropriately.  
• Create new feature variables, which include average daily expenses, total monthly expenditures, number of anomalies recently experienced, among others.

## **Model Requirements**
• Develop at least two machine learning algorithms, for instance, Gradient Boosting Regressor and Linear Regression.
• Train the algorithm for predicting savings estimates and future spending patterns.
• Determine the efficiency of the models with the help of Mean Absolute Error , Mean Squared Error , and R² Score.


## **Output Requirements**
• Generate a prioritized list of users flagged for overspending, including confidence or probability scores. 
• Produce visualizations of key spending trends and savings prediction probabilities.
• Export reports in JSON and HTML formats for easy sharing and archival.

## **Error Handling and Documentation**
• Exception handling must be done to handle issues related to data inconsistencies, invalid formats, and other runtime issues.
 • Code must have modular structure along with proper separation of different modules like loading, preprocessing, feature extraction, modeling, evaluation, and output generation.
 • Code must include comments explaining modeling decisions, assumptions made, and limitation of model.
 • Usage of code must be included in script documentation.


## **Performance and Scalability**
• Implement the system such that it is easily scalable and is able to accommodate many users. 
• Handle the data efficiently by applying efficient querying and paging techniques using the Django ORM.
• Make sure results are replicable by selecting the right random seeds. 
• Construct the system such that other data sources can be added to it in the future.


## **Tools and Libraries**
Install the following modules:
• pandas and numpy for data analysis 
• scikit-learn for building models and evaluation 
• matplotlib/seaborn for data visualization 
• Django framework for web app development 
• Chart.js for frontend data visualization 
• SQLite/PostgreSQL for database management.
